data.content:
**What changed:**
- Constructor accepts an optional `TimeProvider` (defaults to `TimeProvider.System` — zero breaking change for existing callers).
- `IsOverdue` now reads time from `_timeProvider.GetUtcNow()`.

**In tests**, use `Microsoft.Extensions.Time.Testing.FakeTimeProvider` (NuGet: `Microsoft.Extensions.TimeProvider.Testing`):

```csharp
var fake = new FakeTimeProvider(new DateTimeOffset(2025, 1, 1, 0, 0, 0, TimeSpan.Zero));
var calc = new InvoiceCalculator(fake);

Assert.True(calc.IsOverdue(new DateTimeOffset(2024, 12, 31, ...)));
fake.Advance(TimeSpan.FromDays(-365));
Assert.False(calc.IsOverdue(new DateTimeOffset(2024, 12, 31, ...)));
```

No DI container, no custom interfaces — just one built-in abstract class.
